        {
          "question": "q-64554",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+9y=10{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t+\u03d5)+{e}^{-t}$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+\u03d5)+{e}^{-2t}$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t+{e}^{-t}$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $\u03d5$ are constants.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065932/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "c5c7977f8acd2ffcab4719e785af9e89bb1db28b98c19498eaa167529a784d21"
        }
      ],
